From f76151f8d04ff6a7fd22ee821278c408e4610f08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiale Yao <yaojiale_2026@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:23:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: validate RF register response length

The RF register query reads a 32-bit value after an eight-byte response
prefix without checking the skb length. A truncated firmware response
can cause an out-of-bounds read.

Require the prefix and register value before accessing the response.

Fixes: 0a17329ae9c1 ("mt76: mt7915: add debugfs knob for RF registers read/write")
Signed-off-by: Jiale Yao <yaojiale_2026@qq.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/192ec1cd.2297.1a1571ea203.Coremail.yaojiale02@163.com
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 942b0292..066ee1a6 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -4394,6 +4394,10 @@ int mt7915_mcu_rf_regval(struct mt7915_dev *dev, u32 regidx, u32 *val, bool set)
 					&req, sizeof(req), true, &skb);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	if (skb->len < 8 + sizeof(__le32)) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	*val = le32_to_cpu(*(__le32 *)(skb->data + 8));
 	dev_kfree_skb(skb);
